          dealing: 'Each player receives TWO sets of cards: Hand (11-15 cards) and Foot (11-15 cards face-down). Remaining cards form the stock. Top card turned face-up to start discard pile (if Red Three or Wild, bury it and turn another).',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score the most points over 4 rounds by forming melds and canastas. Be the first partnership to go out (empty hand and foot).',
          gameplay: 'Turn Structure: 1. Draw: Draw 2 cards from stock OR pick up entire discard pile (if you can immediately use the top card in a meld). 2. Meld: Lay down melds or add to existing partnership melds. 3. Discard: Discard 1 card to end turn. Minimum Initial Meld: Round 1: 50 points, Round 2: 90 points, Round 3: 120 points, Round 4: 150 points. Picking Up Your Foot: After playing all cards from your hand, pick up your foot. If you discard your last hand card, pick up foot on next turn. If you play all hand cards without discarding, immediately pick up foot and continue playing.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible; if not, may play any card.',
            'Red Threes: +100 points if melded, -100 if caught in hand/foot.',
            'Black Threes: Cannot be melded; -5 points if caught in hand/foot.',
            'Clean Canasta (7 natural cards): +500 points.',
            'Dirty Canasta (with wilds): +300 points.',
            'To go out: Need at least 1 clean and 1 dirty canasta; both partners must have picked up their feet.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on forming canastas quickly. Avoid getting stuck with Red Threes or Black Threes at the end.',
          intermediate: 'Coordinate with your partner. If your partner is close to going out, help them by forming the required canastas.',
          advanced: "Track which cards have been discarded to anticipate what's left in the stock. Time your 'going out' to maximize your score while minimizing opponents' scores.",
          tips: [
            'Red Threes are a double-edged sword: +100 if you go out, -100 if caught.',
            'Black Threes are only useful for blocking the discard pileâ€”discard them when safe.',
            'Clean canastas are worth more than dirty ones. Prioritize them.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
